# The shared libraries the release binaries are allowed to need.
#
# The glibc floor in `linux-baseline` checks symbol versions. This checks the
# other half of "will it start on the baseline": which libraries have to be on
# the host at all. Nothing is bundled (ADR 0023), so every soname here is a
# promise that the baseline distribution already ships it, and docs/release.md
# tells users the same thing.
#
# `build-appimage.sh` reads the direct DT_NEEDED entries of each shipped binary
# and refuses anything not listed, so a dependency that arrives with a crate
# change is a build failure rather than a startup failure on somebody else's
# machine. A soname that stops being needed is not an error; it just makes this
# list larger than it has to be.
#
# Adding a line is a support decision. Change it together with the runtime
# requirements in docs/release.md.

# The C runtime and its compiler support library.
#
# The dynamic linker belongs here too and is deliberately absent: its soname is
# architecture-specific, so packaging/linux-architectures supplies the one the
# build targets and the check adds it to this list. Spelling both out here
# would let a binary built for the wrong architecture pass.
libc.so.6
libm.so.6
libgcc_s.so.1

# Font discovery for the desktop application. It pulls in freetype, libpng,
# expat, zlib, bzip2, and brotli transitively; those are part of the same
# desktop font stack and are not linked directly.
libfontconfig.so.1
